{title: Leaning On The Everlasting Arms}
{key: Ab}

{comment: Verse 1}
[Ab]What a fel-low-ship, [Db]what a joy di-vine,
[Ab]Lean-ing on the ev-er-[Eb]last-ing arms,
[Ab]What a bless-ed-ness, [Db]what a peace is mine,
[Ab]Lean-ing on the ev-er-[Eb]last-ing [Ab]arms.

{comment: Chorus}
[Ab]Lean-ing, [Db]lean-ing, [Ab]Safe and se-cure from [Eb]all a-larms,
[Ab]Lean-ing, [Db]lean-ing, [Ab]lean-ing on the ev-er-[Eb]last-ing [Ab]arms.

{comment: Verse 2}
[Ab]Oh, how sweet to walk [Db]in this pil-grim way,
[Ab]Lean-ing on the ev-er-[Eb]last-ing arms,
[Ab]Oh, how bright the path [Db]grows from day to day,
[Ab]Lean-ing on the ev-er-[Eb]last-ing [Ab]arms.

{comment: Verse 3}
[Ab]What have I to dread, [Db]what have I to fear,
[Ab]Lean-ing on the ev-er-[Eb]last-ing arms?
[Ab]I have bless-ed peace [Db]with my Lord so near,
[Ab]Lean-ing on the ev-er-[Eb]last-ing [Ab]arms.
